=== Timeframe breakdown
--- Timeframe Breakdown
kicker: III. Total Period: 7 Years
scripture: Daniel 9:27 | mark: confirm the covenant with many for one week; in the midst of the week
- The “week” equals 7 prophetic years, calculated as 2,520 days (7 x 360-day lunar year + a “leap month” of 30 days).
stat: 7 | prophetic years
stat: 2,520 | days

--- The days laid side by side
kicker: III. Timeframe Breakdown
image: lessons/prophecy/daniel-8-12-days.svg | The 7-year week of 2,520 days split at the abomination of desolation into two halves of 1,260 days; counted from the abomination, 1,260 days, then 30 more to 1,290, then 45 more to 1,335, the 30 and 45 making 75 days | The week split at the abomination, and the days counted from it ([[Daniel 9:27]]; [[Daniel 12:11-12]])

--- First Half: 3.5 Years
kicker: Tribulation of the Saints, 1,260 Days
scripture: Daniel 7:25 | mark: shall wear out the saints of the most High; until a time and times and the dividing of time
- This period of 1,260 days (3.5 x 360) represents the tribulation where the saints face persecution.

--- Midpoint: Abomination of Desolation
big: Daniel 9:27 | mark: in the midst of the week he shall cause the sacrifice and the oblation to cease, and for the overspreading of abominations he shall make it desolate
- Occurs at the 1,260-day mark, splitting the 7 years.

--- Second Half: 3.5 Years
kicker: Great Tribulation, 1,260 Days + 30 Days
refs: Daniel 7:25
- Extends to 1,290 days:
big: Daniel 12:11 | mark: a thousand two hundred and ninety days
- **Extra 30 Days:** The 1,290 days include the 1,260 days of the second half plus an additional 30 days, likely an intercalary month in the Jewish lunar calendar to align the 360-day prophetic years with the solar calendar, ensuring proper timing of events.

--- Additional 45 Days
kicker: Great Tribulation Concludes
big: Daniel 12:12 | mark: the thousand three hundred and five and thirty days
- The 1,335 days extend 45 days beyond the 1,290 days (1,335 - 1,290 = 45).
stat: 30 | days (1,290 - 1,260)
stat: 45 | days (1,335 - 1,290)
stat: 75 | days
- **Total 75 Days:** The 30 days (1,290 - 1,260) plus 45 days (1,335 - 1,290) form a 75-day period of intensified great tribulation, overlapping the second half’s end, concluding key events.

--- Wrath of God: ~1,185 Days
kicker: Post-1,335 Days
lead: The remaining time after the 1,335 days (approximately 1,185 days, calculated as 2,520 total days minus 1,260 tribulation days and 75 great tribulation days) aligns with the period of God’s wrath, following the conclusion of the great tribulation.

